Measured numbers
================

Microbench (synthetic eth+IPv4+TCP packet, always hits the
fast-path; libflowdis userspace port of the same C code,
gcc -O3, 10M iterations per run):

  uarch              host                            baseline    patched    delta
  -----              ----                            --------    -------    -----
  Zen 2 (4.5 GHz)    Threadripper PRO 3945WX, N=10   12.44 ns    6.56 ns    -47.3 %
  Zen 1 (3.6 GHz)    Ryzen 5 PRO 2400G hp5, N=5      20.50 ns    20.53 ns   within noise

Zen 2 delta is 8 x pooled stdev (highly significant). Zen 1
shows no measurable delta at the median; the ~36 cycle saving
falls below the clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW) timing band
on Zen 1 at this iteration depth. Visible at p10 but not p50.

This is the upper-bound result (one packet shape, always hits
the fast-path). On real traffic with mixed shapes, some packets
fall to the slow path; the average improvement is smaller. The
synthetic upper bound is consistent with kernel projections of
roughly 25-30 % at the median on common internet RX traffic.

Macro tests (60 s, -P 16, sch_cake triple-isolate, tuned TCP,
all combinations IPv4/IPv6 x TCP/UDP x iperf3/iperf2 on two
testbed pairs):

  pair                 Gbit/s baseline (B.1)     Gbit/s patched     delta
  ----                 --------------------       --------------    -----
  mlx5 25 GbE          16.023 (N=279, 24h soak)  15.942 - 16.785   -0.5 % to +4.7 %
  i40e 10 GbE          (no prior baseline)        9.27  -  9.56    near link rate

16 cells total, 0 dmesg WARN/BUG/oops introduced by the patches
on any host across any cell. Full numbers in
perf-results/2026-05-28-series3-phase4/results-full.md on the
flow-keys-compat-reorder branch.


