  - VLAN fast-path (planned for v2).

The non-RFC post will include the soak data and the selftest
output, and update the microbench section with sparse-master
results.


This is sent as RFC for early feedback on:

  - The dispatch shape (single ethertype switch with per-family
    helpers). Is this the right structure?
  - The byte-exact output rule. The alternative is to skip
    "cold" slot writes (saves about 3 ns/pkt) but adds risk if
    a future consumer reads them. v1 chose byte-exact for
    safety; happy to change if reviewers prefer the other rule.
  - The dissector-identity check. A broader rule (any dissector
    whose key set is a subset of what the fast-path writes)
    might catch more callers.

